<%#
Northwestern header. Replaces upstream's modules/_header.html.erb, which is left
in place untouched so it keeps merging cleanly; layouts/avalon.html.erb points
here instead.

Structure is Northwestern's: a dark purple utility bar with the wordmark and
global links, then a purple bar with the site name and search. Styled by
app/assets/stylesheets/northwestern/components/_header.scss.

Two things differ from the 7.x version of this partial:

  * The search box and the sign-in / sign-out links render upstream's
    modules/avalon_search_form and modules/user_management partials rather than
    the hardcoded <form> and link_to the 7.x version carried. Those had drifted:
    the form posted to a literal "/catalog" with no search_field, and neither
    picked up the labels, test ids, or the value round-trip that upstream's
    partials have since grown.

  * No skip link. The 7.x version opened with its own
    `.screen-reader-shortcut` anchor to #main-content; layouts/avalon.html.erb
    already emits one just above this partial, using skip_to_content_href so it
    lands on the player on media object pages.

Everything in here is hidden below the md breakpoint by upstream's
`header div { @extend .mobile-hidden }` (avalon/_header.scss). That is
intentional and long-standing -- on narrow viewports the purple navbar brand row
is the header. See components/_navbar.scss.
%>
<header>
  <div id="top-bar">
    <div class="contain-1120">
      <div id="northwestern">
        <a href="https://www.northwestern.edu/" title="Northwestern University Home"><span class="hide-label">Northwestern University</span></a>
      </div>

      <nav id="global-links" aria-label="global links">
        <ul>
          <li><%= render 'modules/user_management' %></li>
        </ul>
      </nav>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div id="bottom-bar" class="contain-1120">
    <div id="site-name">
      <%= link_to "Libraries - Repository Audio + Video", main_app.root_path %>
    </div>

    <div id="search">
      <%= render partial: 'modules/avalon_search_form' %>
    </div>
  </div>
</header>
